@startuml
title UC-01 - Editable Environment destinations
autonumber
actor Developer as Dev
boundary SettingsController as API
control ApplicationService as Apps
control EnvironmentSettingsService as Settings
control EnvironmentTransitionService as Transition
database UnitOfWork as DB
participant SecretStoreResolver as Stores
participant PostgreSQLTransfer as PG
Dev -> API: CreateApplication(name, subdomain)
API -> Apps: Validate/create identity and two unset Environments
Apps -> DB: Atomic create, no defaults or runtime
Dev -> API: Save initial/change Connection(expectedVersion)
API -> Settings: Scoped validation
Settings -> DB: CAS version, require no active owner
DB --> Dev: New version or 409 stale/busy
Dev -> API: Change secret store(expectedVersion, configVersion)
API -> Settings: Claim operation atomically
Settings -> Stores: Copy immutable desired Secrets and verify
Settings -> DB: Commit store/revision under owner + versions
DB --> Dev: Pending Preview/Deploy or safe failure
Dev -> API: Preview target migration(destination, mappings)
API -> Transition: Validate complete snapshot/capability
Transition --> Dev: Pinned token and downtime impact
Dev -> API: Execute(token, acknowledgeDowntime)
API -> Transition: Admit snapshot and claim owner atomically
Transition -> PG: Quiesce writers; backup; provision; restore; verify
Transition -> Transition: Full redeploy, readiness, route cutover
Transition -> DB: Commit destination/current Set; retain source generation
DB --> Dev: Result/progress/recovery, no secret bytes
note over Transition,DB
Network calls outside transactions.
Settings/config/draft writes blocked only while operation owns Environment.
Old targets retained for explicit recovery/cleanup.
end note
@enduml
